    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d318-a4">

                <pb facs="0528" n="416" sameAs="frus:frus1907p1/pg416"/>

                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Inclosure 4.]</seg></opener>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Ambassador McCormick
                        to the Minister for Foreign Affairs</hi>.</head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >American Embassy</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                            >Paris</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian" when="1907-01-21"
                                ><hi rendition="#italic">January 21,
                    1907</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I have the honor to acknowledge the receipt
                    of your excellency’s dispatch of the 18th instant with reference to the case of
                    Jacobs, the American citizen who was arrested on the 4th of December last and
                    who is still confined, this 21st of January, without any action having been
                    taken in the matter.</p>
                <p>I infer from the contents of this note that the Government of the French Republic
                    proposes to surrender this American citizen to the Argentine authorities without
                    putting the American Government in position to ascertain whether it has any
                    objection to this extradition.</p>
                <p>I would be obliged to your excellency to kindly let me know whether such is his
                    intention.</p>
                <p>I avail, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Robert S.
                    McCormick.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
